elds [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33aed63a-b507-5f47-be6d-1ea1968fc56e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33aed63a-b507-5f47-be6d-1ea1968fc56e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232861} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3a34980-8785-53b7-9d2d-c2704de01739" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232860}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7478ba97-dd0a-53c5-98ba-0b472abb594d" :question/math-academy-id "q-342142" :question/problem "Find the slope ${m}^{'}$ of the normal line to the curve $y=4-3{x}^{2}$ at the point $(1,1).$\n\n${m}^{'}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=4-3{x}^{2}.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n{f}^{'}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4-3{x}^{2})=-6x\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(1,1):$\n\n$$\nm={f}^{'}(1)=-6(1)=-6\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope ${m}^{'}$ of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{'} & =-\\frac{1}{m} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(-6)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233925 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7785e0f8-d36d-58f1-b4bb-92dad6d81157" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232863}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7785e0f8-d36d-58f1-b4bb-92dad6d81157" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232863} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed26559a-60f3-5110-9c11-8fb12d780195" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232862}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "31e569a8-362b-51d8-8186-4764daa7d587" :question/math-academy-id "q-342147" :question/problem "Find the slope ${m}^{'}$ of the normal line to the curve $y=\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{5}-4{x}^{2}$ at the point $(2,-8).$\n\n${m}^{'}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{5}-4{x}^{2}.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n{f}^{'}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{5}-4{x}^{2}\\right)=\\frac{5}{4}{x}^{4}-8x\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(2,-8):$\n\n$$\nm={f}^{'}(2)=\\frac{5}{4}({2}^{4})-8(2)=20-16=4\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope ${m}^{'}$ of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{'} & =-\\frac{1}{m} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233926 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91f91eef-b83d-531e-8528-82c356da256b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232865}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91f91eef-b83d-531e-8528-82c356da256b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232865} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4685f24-ff78-51cf-b109-1a2be8dffda8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232864}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ff198fc0-46a3-5bea-900f-f995439b9d1c" :question/math-academy-id "q-342152" :question/problem "Find the slope ${m}^{'}$ of the normal line to the curve $y=2{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}$ at the point $(-1,-3).$\n\n${m}^{'}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=2{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(2{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}-{x}^{-4}) \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}+4{x}^{-5} \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}+\\frac{4}{{x}^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(-1,-3):$\n\n$$\nm={f}^{'}(-1)=6{(-1)}^{2}+\\frac{4}{(-1)^{5}}=6-4=2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope ${m}^{'}$ of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{'} & =-\\frac{1}{m} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234307 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9e0de752-0812-5082-ba75-5deee887ec8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-71525" :question/problem "Find the slope of the normal line to the curve $y=2{x}^{3}-x+3$ at the point $(1,4).$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=2{x}^{3}-x+3.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}-x+3)=6{x}^{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(1,4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{'}(1)=6(1)-1=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line ${m}^{'}$ is\n\n$$\n{m}^{'}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{5}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238012 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e0dfaf6-4b26-5780-916c-6b6e7cc84e78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236012} {:answer/id #uuid "a04d6a2e-4584-529d-a61d-427012951a99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236818} {:answer/id #uuid "d1ea2eb4-6e83-5f3b-a04e-b53fcabdb24e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237145} {:answer/id #uuid "e1e93d2c-4a24-59ba-9508-adf45fe9d13a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237231} {:answer/id #uuid "ebfbd345-bc08-5590-b695-612eea6c6693" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1e93d2c-4a24-59ba-9508-adf45fe9d13a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237231} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fea9d47-2732-52fb-98f5-f254a1901480" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237505}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "27376e81-fcda-5685-8dbf-1c9048989040" :question/math-academy-id "q-103531" :question/problem "Find the slope of the normal line to the curve $y=2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}-2{x}^{2}$ at the point $(1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}-2{x}^{2}.$ Computing the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}-2{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3/2}-2{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{1/2}-4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute ${f}^{′}(1)$, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1)=3(1)^{1/2}-4(1)=-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line ${m}^{′}$ is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238013 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e61460f-455d-520d-93b5-dffbbc89788f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236320} {:answer/id #uuid "69eb4aac-b14f-57bd-a480-1ab582de3ba8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236485} {:answer/id #uuid "6f3b9c84-9c83-5f6f-86e3-c86711996c77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236519} {:answer/id #uuid "86d05e0e-a4ab-5588-b9b4-148c9e0ee1d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236656} {:answer/id #uuid "cb23d69f-8e38-59d2-a2f7-6d29f4a5143d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237106}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb23d69f-8e38-59d2-a2f7-6d29f4a5143d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237106} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9fd797f-3553-5404-8639-7c51e487bdfc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237766}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "64a70883-2f1e-5226-9a93-f2c233eeb60b" :question/math-academy-id "q-103532" :question/problem "Find the slope of the normal line to the curve $y={x}^{3}-4\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}$ at the point $(1,-3).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)={x}^{3}-4\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}.$ Computing the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}-4\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}-4{x}^{5/2}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}-10{x}^{3/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute ${f}^{′}(1)$, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1)=3(1)^{2}-10(1)^{3/2}=-7\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line  ${m}^{′}$ is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=\\frac{1}{7}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238019 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0de724df-8b1c-5535-8e44-daf76049ece3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235891} {:answer/id #uuid "23b48bbe-ffa7-54a8-99f9-dc3950946ae0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236047} {:answer/id #uuid "4e607467-80e3-56bc-b439-ef24f59e6ec4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236319} {:answer/id #uuid "b66f9765-eff6-521c-bc5e-6e7d22591dfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236972} {:answer/id #uuid "ce4263ad-8b05-53b5-bdc9-5ccb768cb0a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e607467-80e3-56bc-b439-ef24f59e6ec4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236319} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fef744c-c73f-546c-b977-0ab52629ab8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237630}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "602176f6-b1e0-573b-b42a-73b7532c22d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-103543" :question/problem "Find the slope of the normal line to the curve $y=\\frac{2}{{x}^{5}}+7x$ at the point $(1,9).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{5}}+7x.$ Computing the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{2}{{x}^{5}}+7x\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{-5}+7x) \\\\  & =-10{x}^{-6}+7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute ${f}^{′}(1)$, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1)=-10(1)^{-6}+7=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line ${m}^{′}$ is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317210 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67ba581c-ebc6-55ea-99ee-e980b997d941" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315698}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67ba581c-ebc6-55ea-99ee-e980b997d941" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315698} :answer-field/id #uuid "fea3ff45-b371-5b5e-8ab3-a1c221cf4178" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317154}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2cc6d36c-e26a-5fcd-bcb0-d88e0fe39c17" :question/math-academy-id "q-342153" :question/problem "Find the slope ${m}^{′}$ of the normal line to the curve $y=4-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}$ at the point $\\left(\\frac{1}{4},2\\right).$\n\n${m}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=4-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(4-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4-{x}^{-1/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $\\left(\\frac{1}{4},2\\right):$\n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)}^{3}}}=4\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope ${m}^{′}$ of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{′} & =-\\frac{1}{m} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329815 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "298a6c80-4207-50f6-8a34-1d93a5f89fed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327287} {:answer/id #uuid "307e57c3-1572-5e33-a5f9-3472b90bf91f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327363} {:answer/id #uuid "e1ee7da7-a08a-5f34-86ea-f3f106a5f98c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328912} {:answer/id #uuid "e33c1589-993a-5e15-9743-78a5a9f95009" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328926} {:answer/id #uuid "fb9c839b-8755-5fd8-b8d8-b4929a06d14c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb9c839b-8755-5fd8-b8d8-b4929a06d14c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329142} :answer-field/id #uuid "197f2e71-4c00-5a81-830b-269b6b29fd90" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329228}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "704dafc6-9839-55e3-9683-dc5e275270d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-47449" :question/problem "Find the slope of the normal line to the curve $y={x}^{2}+x$ at the point $(1,2).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)={x}^{2}+x.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+x) \\\\  & =2x+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(1,2):$\n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}(1)=2(1)+1=3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line ${m}^{′}$ is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338957 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "105a0ee2-ecfe-5f6b-abf3-c2b8990ff5e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336186} {:answer/id #uuid "8afbf511-93b1-574c-aea0-f719ed534072" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337288} {:answer/id #uuid "9b55a9ee-2b2e-5710-b96a-5529ce814f84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337440} {:answer/id #uuid "b83a05a7-995d-5078-bf9a-4b58abb10a90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337665} {:answer/id #uuid "e2cfabde-266f-53a5-a5bf-2a8c9659561a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "105a0ee2-ecfe-5f6b-abf3-c2b8990ff5e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336186} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb39a159-1af8-51a3-9955-b31d00f03bbf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338721}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0b93f0c3-f4cf-5391-8374-d4b6970c54ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-71524" :question/problem "Find the slope of the normal line to the curve $y={x}^{2}-5$ at the point $(2,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)={x}^{2}-5.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}-5)=2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(2,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{′}(2)=2(2)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line ${m}^{′}$ is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524012 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a4af37e-6b2f-57b0-a6f0-ff63aa93a160" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523376} {:answer/id #uuid "3b6dcd76-9c75-5cab-a7e3-98ec9a075e7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523378} {:answer/id #uuid "8e9d1766-796c-5f7e-b81b-0f2e720704a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523551} {:answer/id #uuid "f09476ea-f87a-5f66-921f-9f3fefea5c34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523757} {:answer/id #uuid "fbd47810-d0f2-5cff-a8e5-e4945ca20335" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523781}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e9d1766-796c-5f7e-b81b-0f2e720704a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523551} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c700890-f7ec-5058-9334-5a60b70722d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523850}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ccfa4d84-7836-5556-9446-f447928d0c91" :question/math-academy-id "q-103539" :question/problem "Find the slope of the normal line to the curve $y=\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}}+\\frac{x}{2}$ at the point $\\left(-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{4}\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}}+\\frac{x}{2}.$ Computing the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}}+\\frac{x}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-3}+\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute ${f}^{′}\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right),$ which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{-3}+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line ${m}^{′}$ is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{2}{9}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524021 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54c886c0-75b9-56f6-8629-ffc88d7f38eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523425} {:answer/id #uuid "7676dc7b-ce9f-5ee4-b0f0-1d0b1d1ad93a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523496} {:answer/id #uuid "9992b9e3-55cb-534c-8fd0-21fbd64e8078" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523573} {:answer/id #uuid "d57dc05b-2779-515b-aecf-82edefe5f6a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523702} {:answer/id #uuid "f442a990-1c89-5b31-9a80-2c9fda10deea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523763}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7676dc7b-ce9f-5ee4-b0f0-1d0b1d1ad93a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523496} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa8e2a76-bef8-546c-bf0c-5ea711bff307" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523917}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e108591f-1dbb-58f4-aca2-6f29ab0389ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-71526" :question/problem "Find the slope of the normal line to the curve $y=2{x}^{3}-7x$ at the point $(-1,5).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=2{x}^{3}-7x.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}-7x)=6{x}^{2}-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(-1,5):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{′}(-1)=6(-1)^{2}-7=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line ${m}^{′}$ is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{(-1)}=1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186710692 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f0f9a14-e0cb-55fa-971a-08e33d7ad976" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710693} {:answer/id #uuid "94eca3fc-ae43-5ca3-b806-dad759ed9995" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710700} {:answer/id #uuid "a2565dc8-3877-5798-9f0a-7a20e48eec4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710701} {:answer/id #uuid "a6a01cfa-532a-58cc-bf13-3d9bc4fe5be4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710702} {:answer/id #uuid "c67b0b94-c705-5bb1-846a-3c68755c080e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710703}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94eca3fc-ae43-5ca3-b806-dad759ed9995" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710700} :answer-field/id #uuid "e63039b4-efb2-5ec3-b9cd-123073b36c16" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710704}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1029b6ff-8883-5073-891f-983a0a0dd842" :question/problem "Find the slope of the normal line to the curve $y=x^2-5x+1$ at the point $(1,-3)$." :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=x^2-5x+1$. First, compute the derivative:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=2x-5.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent at $(1,-3)$ is\n\n$$\nm=f'(1)=2(1)-5=-3.\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so its slope is the negative reciprocal:\n\n$$\nm'=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{-3}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nThe diagram shows the tangent and the dashed normal meeting at the given point.\n\n![The curve with its tangent and dashed normal at P.](images/bb/bb940c649033bddbbc6d8c3d96c73fc66c62fc4664481dabfeeb7a63daa872d4.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186710695 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ede11da-1365-53da-a4f1-25d88e85ab1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{39}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710696}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ede11da-1365-53da-a4f1-25d88e85ab1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{39}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710696} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c52d80b-cda4-56b7-b24f-b8483b38851d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710697}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "41907510-4e56-5323-b592-bd080fe7b53e" :question/problem "Find the slope $m'$ of the normal line to the curve\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{(x-1)^2}{\\sqrt{x}},\\qquad x>0,\n$$\n\nat the point $\\left(4,\\frac{9}{2}\\right)$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$m'=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=\\dfrac{(x-1)^2}{\\sqrt{x}}$. Expand the numerator and divide each term by $x^{1/2}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=\\frac{x^2-2x+1}{x^{1/2}}\\\\\n&=x^{3/2}-2x^{1/2}+x^{-1/2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the power rule to all three terms:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=\\frac{3}{2}x^{1/2}-x^{-1/2}-\\frac{1}{2}x^{-3/2}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent at $\\left(4,\\frac{9}{2}\\right)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm=f'(4)&=\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{4}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4}}-\\frac{1}{2(4)^{3/2}}\\\\\n&=3-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{16}\\\\\n&=\\frac{39}{16}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe normal has the negative reciprocal slope:\n\n$$\nm'=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{39/16}=-\\frac{16}{39}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186710698 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c5d459e-fc67-5800-9475-effc23a28a9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710694}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c5d459e-fc67-5800-9475-effc23a28a9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710694} :answer-field/id #uuid "699f3137-302f-535e-9a25-2d62b72d6d63" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710699}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "62821c03-5ce7-5c40-8dad-648f01cba324" :question/problem "Find the slope $m'$ of the normal line to the curve $y=(x+1)(x^2-2x)$ at the point $(2,0)$.\n\n$m'=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=(x+1)(x^2-2x)$. Expand before differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=x^3-2x^2+x^2-2x\\\\\n&=x^3-x^2-2x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the power rule:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=3x^2-2x-2.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent at $(2,0)$ is\n\n$$\nm=f'(2)=3(2)^2-2(2)-2=12-4-2=6.\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent. Therefore,\n\n$$\nm'=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186710928 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "887d9d0b-a070-5758-800a-491a7fc379b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710938} {:answer/id #uuid "3d514e71-bd7c-4ef2-9ca8-91034d24e007" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186760392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "887d9d0b-a070-5758-800a-491a7fc379b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710938} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1e7d706-7ec4-5336-a848-2786deb7472a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710942}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "189f6de7-6cdc-55b9-82f9-8c9a94482be0" :question/problem "Find the slope $m'$ of the normal line to the curve\n\n$$\ny=3x^{2}\n$$\n\nat the point $\\left(-2,12\\right)$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$m'=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=3x^{2}$.\n\nApply the power rule:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=6x\n$$\n\nThe tangent slope at $\\left(-2,12\\right)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm=f'(-2)&=6\\left(-2\\right)\\\\\n&=-12\\\\\n&=-12\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so take the negative reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm'&=-\\frac{1}{m}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{\\left(-12\\right)}\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{12}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186710929 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6bc851da-6370-5083-9183-d4e9a53b4abf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bc851da-6370-5083-9183-d4e9a53b4abf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710935} :answer-field/id #uuid "904a35f2-0b11-5bdc-b371-366dda504f84" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710939}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "24f2d725-a991-56e8-97f8-433f79882c73" :question/problem "Find the slope $m'$ of the normal line to the curve\n\n$$\ny=x^{2}-x+2\n$$\n\nat the point $\\left(2,4\\right)$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$m'=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=x^{2}-x+2$.\n\nApply the power rule:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=2x-1\n$$\n\nThe tangent slope at $\\left(2,4\\right)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm=f'(2)&=2\\left(2\\right)-1\\\\\n&=4-1\\\\\n&=3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so take the negative reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm'&=-\\frac{1}{m}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{\\left(3\\right)}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186710931 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c314992-062b-5890-955c-6d425dbd55c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710930}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c314992-062b-5890-955c-6d425dbd55c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710930} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c42c69f-56c2-546a-a501-4919ce7b8cc9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710936}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "49112d0c-3d7c-525f-9985-5e6477ab4831" :question/problem "Find the slope $m'$ of the normal line to the curve\n\n$$\ny=2x^{2}+4x\n$$\n\nat the point $\\left(-2,0\\right)$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$m'=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=2x^{2}+4x$.\n\nApply the power rule:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=4x+4\n$$\n\nThe tangent slope at $\\left(-2,0\\right)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm=f'(-2)&=4\\left(-2\\right)+4\\\\\n&=-8+4\\\\\n&=-4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so take the negative reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm'&=-\\frac{1}{m}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{\\left(-4\\right)}\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186710932 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bcdb7be-aac3-5270-8a55-f400c665daea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bcdb7be-aac3-5270-8a55-f400c665daea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710937} :answer-field/id #uuid "56e75578-ce23-573f-89a0-df585996e8b7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710933}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4b9563ef-5cbb-5c4b-94e8-911e07e06551" :question/problem "Find the slope $m'$ of the normal line to the curve\n\n$$\ny=-3x^{2}-3x-1\n$$\n\nat the point $\\left(1,-7\\right)$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$m'=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=-3x^{2}-3x-1$.\n\nApply the power rule:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=-6x-3\n$$\n\nThe tangent slope at $\\left(1,-7\\right)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm=f'(1)&=-6\\left(1\\right)-3\\\\\n&=-6-3\\\\\n&=-9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so take the negative reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm'&=-\\frac{1}{m}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{\\left(-9\\right)}\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{9}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186710941 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6903a7c7-2ab4-5b23-a072-26c2e30b900f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710934}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6903a7c7-2ab4-5b23-a072-26c2e30b900f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710934} :answer-field/id #uuid "985c8402-6ac9-5095-b6b1-c6392b50d1ad" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710940}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b614ee37-cd64-5dd4-a877-92acf81cc12b" :question/problem "Find the slope $m'$ of the normal line to the curve\n\n$$\ny=x^{2}+5x+1\n$$\n\nat the point $\\left(1,7\\right)$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$m'=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=x^{2}+5x+1$.\n\nApply the power rule:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=2x+5\n$$\n\nThe tangent slope at $\\left(1,7\\right)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm=f'(1)&=2\\left(1\\right)+5\\\\\n&=2+5\\\\\n&=7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so take the negative reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm'&=-\\frac{1}{m}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{\\left(7\\right)}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{7}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186710944 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ed80582-ba8a-5f2b-a20c-6b7c23fd959e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{55}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ed80582-ba8a-5f2b-a20c-6b7c23fd959e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{55}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710949} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b608208-a9f7-5e42-af2d-6573b72464e9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710950}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "13b562cc-e2c6-5d87-b19a-0abf685228cd" :question/problem "Find the slope $m'$ of the normal line to the curve\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{(x+1)^2}{\\sqrt{x}},\\qquad x>0\n$$\n\nat the point $\\left(4,-\\frac{25}{2}\\right)$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$m'=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=-\\frac{(x+1)^2}{\\sqrt{x}}$. Expand the numerator and divide each term by $x^{1/2}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=\\frac{-x^{2}-2x-1}{x^{1/2}}\\\\\n&=-x^{\\frac{3}{2}}-2x^{\\frac{1}{2}}-x^{-\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the power rule:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=-\\frac{3}{2}x^{\\frac{1}{2}}-x^{-\\frac{1}{2}}+\\frac{1}{2}x^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\n$$\n\nThe tangent slope at $\\left(4,-\\frac{25}{2}\\right)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm=f'(4)&=-\\frac{3}{2}\\left(4\\right)^{\\frac{1}{2}}-\\left(4\\right)^{-\\frac{1}{2}}+\\frac{1}{2}\\left(4\\right)^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\\\\\n&=-3-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{16}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{55}{16}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so take the negative reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm'&=-\\frac{1}{m}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{\\left(-\\frac{55}{16}\\right)}\\\\\n&=\\frac{16}{55}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186710945 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0c41fff-6dd6-5636-ae22-a23f175263e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710952} {:answer/id #uuid "cb8f86e3-b9d7-453c-8427-64615f8e6657" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{14+2\\sqrt3}{46}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186760397}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0c41fff-6dd6-5636-ae22-a23f175263e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710952} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1627a85-1cc6-582e-8c15-1971b8792a1a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710955}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1b487f77-15da-5b78-b3ec-52fe09ab20aa" :question/problem "Find the slope $m'$ of the normal line to the curve\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{(x-3)^2}{\\sqrt{x}},\\qquad x>0\n$$\n\nat the point $\\left(9,12\\right)$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$m'=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=\\frac{(x-3)^2}{\\sqrt{x}}$. Expand the numerator and divide each term by $x^{1/2}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=\\frac{x^{2}-6x+9}{x^{1/2}}\\\\\n&=x^{\\frac{3}{2}}-6x^{\\frac{1}{2}}+9x^{-\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the power rule:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=\\frac{3}{2}x^{\\frac{1}{2}}-3x^{-\\frac{1}{2}}-\\frac{9}{2}x^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\n$$\n\nThe tangent slope at $\\left(9,12\\right)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm=f'(9)&=\\frac{3}{2}\\left(9\\right)^{\\frac{1}{2}}-3\\left(9\\right)^{-\\frac{1}{2}}-\\frac{9}{2}\\left(9\\right)^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\\\\\n&=\\frac{9}{2}-1-\\frac{1}{6}\\\\\n&=\\frac{10}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so take the negative reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm'&=-\\frac{1}{m}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{10}{3}\\right)}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{3}{10}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186710953 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2340e802-e6e0-588a-8a1b-6d34e4e65862" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710946}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2340e802-e6e0-588a-8a1b-6d34e4e65862" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710946} :answer-field/id #uuid "45932cc5-5994-5471-b9ce-40bb399d9425" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710948}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bbcc2c19-ad0a-5a30-bf14-1b8dab59e864" :question/problem "Find the slope $m'$ of the normal line to the curve\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{(x-2)^2}{\\sqrt{x}},\\qquad x>0\n$$\n\nat the point $\\left(4,2\\right)$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$m'=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=\\frac{(x-2)^2}{\\sqrt{x}}$. Expand the numerator and divide each term by $x^{1/2}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=\\frac{x^{2}-4x+4}{x^{1/2}}\\\\\n&=x^{\\frac{3}{2}}-4x^{\\frac{1}{2}}+4x^{-\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the power rule:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=\\frac{3}{2}x^{\\frac{1}{2}}-2x^{-\\frac{1}{2}}-2x^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\n$$\n\nThe tangent slope at $\\left(4,2\\right)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm=f'(4)&=\\frac{3}{2}\\left(4\\right)^{\\frac{1}{2}}-2\\left(4\\right)^{-\\frac{1}{2}}-2\\left(4\\right)^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\\\\\n&=3-1-\\frac{1}{4}\\\\\n&=\\frac{7}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so take the negative reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm'&=-\\frac{1}{m}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{7}{4}\\right)}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{4}{7}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186710954 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4948445-996b-52ec-af10-99e8ae46667b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{54}{275}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4948445-996b-52ec-af10-99e8ae46667b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{54}{275}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710951} :answer-field/id #uuid "424bd42b-f667-5dd3-a87e-814553941f00" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710947}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c2bfa780-9936-5b1d-9e9b-31c2913c438d" :question/problem "Find the slope $m'$ of the normal line to the curve\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{(x+2)^2}{\\sqrt{x}},\\qquad x>0\n$$\n\nat the point $\\left(9,\\frac{121}{3}\\right)$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$m'=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=\\frac{(x+2)^2}{\\sqrt{x}}$. Expand the numerator and divide each term by $x^{1/2}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=\\frac{x^{2}+4x+4}{x^{1/2}}\\\\\n&=x^{\\frac{3}{2}}+4x^{\\frac{1}{2}}+4x^{-\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the power rule:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=\\frac{3}{2}x^{\\frac{1}{2}}+2x^{-\\frac{1}{2}}-2x^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\n$$\n\nThe tangent slope at $\\left(9,\\frac{121}{3}\\right)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm=f'(9)&=\\frac{3}{2}\\left(9\\right)^{\\frac{1}{2}}+2\\left(9\\right)^{-\\frac{1}{2}}-2\\left(9\\right)^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\\\\\n&=\\frac{9}{2}+\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{2}{27}\\\\\n&=\\frac{275}{54}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so take the negative reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm'&=-\\frac{1}{m}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{275}{54}\\right)}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{54}{275}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186710957 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d1e857e-fa9c-547e-9986-65d580e9e1f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710956}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d1e857e-fa9c-547e-9986-65d580e9e1f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710956} :answer-field/id #uuid "faae9f6c-dd6e-5f95-b876-4badfc619def" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710967}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "21b31e91-7538-5cc3-90e2-12eb2f4f2d4c" :question/problem "Find the slope $m'$ of the normal line to the curve\n\n$$\ny=(x+3)(x^{2}+x)\n$$\n\nat the point $\\left(-1,0\\right)$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$m'=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=(x+3)(x^{2}+x)$. Expand and combine like terms before differentiating.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=x^{3}+x^{2}+3x^{2}+3x\\\\\n&=x^{3}+4x^{2}+3x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the power rule:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=3x^{2}+8x+3\n$$\n\nThe tangent slope at $\\left(-1,0\\right)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm=f'(-1)&=3\\left(-1\\right)^{2}+8\\left(-1\\right)+3\\\\\n&=3-8+3\\\\\n&=-2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so take the negative reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm'&=-\\frac{1}{m}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{\\left(-2\\right)}\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186710960 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd2ce276-042e-576e-874b-b398f8c7af88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd2ce276-042e-576e-874b-b398f8c7af88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710965} :answer-field/id #uuid "7479c0dd-fde8-5f16-a231-35d74d856bee" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710961}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6acc9a6b-1408-5ff3-88af-47a8f8d86ef3" :question/problem "Find the slope $m'$ of the normal line to the curve\n\n$$\ny=(x-2)(x^{2}+x)\n$$\n\nat the point $\\left(-2,-8\\right)$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$m'=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=(x-2)(x^{2}+x)$. Expand and combine like terms before differentiating.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=x^{3}+x^{2}-2x^{2}-2x\\\\\n&=x^{3}-x^{2}-2x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the power rule:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=3x^{2}-2x-2\n$$\n\nThe tangent slope at $\\left(-2,-8\\right)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm=f'(-2)&=3\\left(-2\\right)^{2}-2\\left(-2\\right)-2\\\\\n&=12+4-2\\\\\n&=14\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so take the negative reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm'&=-\\frac{1}{m}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{\\left(14\\right)}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{14}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186710963 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4684235a-039e-55e0-a551-2d96b395ba1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710959} {:answer/id #uuid "c48ab8d5-24fa-4b52-8349-32f89029e2a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186760401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4684235a-039e-55e0-a551-2d96b395ba1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710959} :answer-field/id #uuid "31315585-aaf4-5656-ac0b-c11d323fd370" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710958}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b303525d-fa10-553d-bfb9-c9d415e56059" :question/problem "Find the slope $m'$ of the normal line to the curve\n\n$$\ny=(x+1)(x^{2}+2x)\n$$\n\nat the point $\\left(-2,0\\right)$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$m'=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=(x+1)(x^{2}+2x)$. Expand and combine like terms before differentiating.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=x^{3}+2x^{2}+x^{2}+2x\\\\\n&=x^{3}+3x^{2}+2x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the power rule:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=3x^{2}+6x+2\n$$\n\nThe tangent slope at $\\left(-2,0\\right)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm=f'(-2)&=3\\left(-2\\right)^{2}+6\\left(-2\\right)+2\\\\\n&=12-12+2\\\\\n&=2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so take the negative reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm'&=-\\frac{1}{m}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{\\left(2\\right)}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186710964 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d59fcf47-af54-571d-93e8-31b1baefde00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710966} {:answer/id #uuid "40c93d4d-5e53-4735-9a43-3d944a65f7dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186760404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d59fcf47-af54-571d-93e8-31b1baefde00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710966} :answer-field/id #uuid "965af6c2-93c4-51e9-b54a-ffd415552d5c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186710962}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bb66e871-f275-5437-9e35-67e011b9fc64" :question/problem "Find the slope $m'$ of the normal line to the curve\n\n$$\ny=(x+2)(x^{2}-2x)\n$$\n\nat the point $\\left(2,0\\right)$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$m'=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=(x+2)(x^{2}-2x)$. Expand and combine like terms before differentiating.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=x^{3}-2x^{2}+2x^{2}-4x\\\\\n&=x^{3}-4x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the power rule:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=3x^{2}-4\n$$\n\nThe tangent slope at $\\left(2,0\\right)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm=f'(2)&=3\\left(2\\right)^{2}-4\\\\\n&=12-4\\\\\n&=8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so take the negative reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm'&=-\\frac{1}{m}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{\\left(8\\right)}\\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{8}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of a Normal Line to a Curve at a Point"}]}
